# Sugar Count — Personal Web App (PWA) Spec

## Overview
Sugar Count is a personal web app for tracking which days I eat sugar and/or
carbs. It is only for me. I will open it in Safari on my iPhone and use
"Add to Home Screen", so it must behave like a native app: full-screen,
works offline, and has its own icon. No accounts, no backend, no analytics,
no network calls after the first load.

Keep it simple: two screens, local storage only, cute UI in green and white.

## Tech stack
- Plain HTML, CSS, and vanilla JavaScript (ES modules). No framework, no build step.
- Chart: Chart.js loaded from a pinned CDN version, OR vendored locally into
  /vendor so the app works fully offline (preferred: vendored).
- Storage: IndexedDB (small wrapper), with localStorage only for tiny settings.
- PWA: manifest.webmanifest + service worker that caches all app files
  (cache-first) so it opens with no internet.
- Hosting: static files, deployable to GitHub Pages. Include a short README
  with deploy steps and the "Add to Home Screen" steps on iPhone.

