## iOS home screen requirements
In index.html <head>:
- <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover">
- <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
- <meta name="mobile-web-app-capable" content="yes">
- <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-status-bar-style" content="default">
- <meta name="apple-mobile-web-app-title" content="Sugar Count">
- <meta name="theme-color" content="#4DB57A">
- <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="icons/apple-touch-icon.png">
- <link rel="manifest" href="manifest.webmanifest">
Manifest: name and short_name "Sugar Count", display "standalone",
background_color "#F4FBF6", theme_color "#4DB57A", the 192 and 512 icons.
Respect safe areas with env(safe-area-inset-*) so nothing sits under the
notch or home indicator. Disable double-tap zoom and text selection on buttons.

## Data model
One record per calendar day, keyed by local date string "YYYY-MM-DD"
(never store timezone-shifted timestamps):

{ date: "2026-10-14", ateSugar: boolean, ateCarbs: boolean, note: string }

Rules:
- A day with NO record is a CLEAN day (no sugar, no carbs).
- Only store a record when the day has sugar, carbs, or a note.
  If I turn both toggles off and clear the note, delete the record.
- Tracking start date: stored in settings, defaults to the date the app is
  first opened. Days before the start date are not counted anywhere and
  show as neutral (no indicator) on the calendar. I can change the start
  date in a small settings sheet.
- Future dates are not counted and cannot be edited.
- Any past day from the start date up to today can be added or edited at any time.

## Navigation
Bottom tab bar with two tabs: "Calendar" and "Summary". Simple inline SVG
icons. Active tab in primary green.

## Screen 1: Calendar (main screen)
- Month grid, Monday first. Header with month and year, prev/next buttons,
  swipe left/right to change month, and a "Today" button.
- Day cell indicators:
  - Sugar eaten: pink dot
  - Carbs eaten: amber dot
  - Both: both dots
  - Clean (no record, within tracking range, not in future): small green leaf
  - Has a note: tiny underline or corner mark
  - Before start date or in the future: dimmed, no indicator
- Today has a green ring.
- Tapping a day opens a bottom sheet:
  - Title: formatted date, e.g. "Tuesday, Oct 14"
  - Two big pill toggles: "Sugar" and "Carbs" (filled when on)
  - One-line text input: "Add a note (optional)", max 100 characters
  - "Save" button. "Reset to clean" button shown only if a record exists.
  - Tapping outside or swiping down closes without saving.
- Below the calendar: a small legend and a this-month line,
  e.g. "Sugar 6 days, Carbs 11 days, Clean 9 days".
- Small gear icon in the header opens settings: tracking start date,
  Export data (downloads a JSON file), Import data (from that JSON file).

## Screen 2: Summary
- Segmented control: "4 weeks" | "3 months" | "Year"
  - 4 weeks and 3 months: one point per week
  - Year: one point per month
- Line chart with two lines: sugar days per period and carb days per period.
  Colors match the calendar dots, smooth curves (tension ~0.35), round point
  markers, legend, Y axis starts at 0 with whole numbers only.
  Partial periods (current week/month, or periods cut by the start date)
  only count days inside the tracking range.
- Under the chart, small rounded stat tiles:
  - Sugar days in range
  - Carb days in range
  - Current sugar-free streak (consecutive days ending today with no sugar,
    not going before the start date)
  - Current carb-free streak
- If the start date is today and nothing is logged, show a friendly empty
  state: "Tap a day on the calendar to log it."

## Visual design
- Green and white. Background #F4FBF6, cards white, primary green #4DB57A,
  dark green text #1F5E3B, light green fills #DDF3E5, sugar pink #F7A8B8,
  carb amber #F2C46D.
- Match the app icon's style: soft, rounded, friendly. Rounded corners
  (sheets 24px, pills fully round, day cells 12px), very soft shadows.
- Font: system rounded stack:
  ui-rounded, "SF Pro Rounded", -apple-system, system-ui, sans-serif.
- Show the sugar-cube icon (icons/icon.svg) small in the calendar header.
- Gentle motion only on user actions: sheet slides up, toggle pills
  bounce slightly when tapped. Respect prefers-reduced-motion.
- Support dark mode via prefers-color-scheme with a dark green/charcoal palette.
- Tap targets at least 44px.

## Done when
- Opens from the home screen full-screen with the provided icon, no Safari UI.
- Works with airplane mode on after the first load.
- I can add and edit any past day since the start date, and unlogged days
  show as clean.
- Calendar and Summary update immediately after saving.
- Data survives closing the app and restarting the phone.
- Export/import round-trips my data correctly.